Riverdale Science Museum
Visitor Basics

Riverdale Science Museum is a small teaching museum in Riverdale. These notes explain how to plan a visit. The same museum is described in the exhibit hall PDF and in the programs Word document.

Opening hours
The museum is open Tuesday through Friday from 9:30 a.m. to 6:00 p.m.
On Saturday the museum is open from 10:00 a.m. to 6:00 p.m.
On Sunday the museum is open from 11:00 a.m. to 5:00 p.m.
The museum is closed on Monday, Thanksgiving Day, and December 25.
The last entry of the day is 45 minutes before closing. On Sunday, last entry is 4:15 p.m.

Tickets
General admission is 14 dollars for adults and 9 dollars for visitors age 6 to 17.
Children age 5 and under enter free with a ticketed adult.
Teachers with a school ID receive free admission for themselves when they bring a class.
Tickets can be bought at the front desk or reserved online under the name Riverdale Science Museum Tickets.
The front desk phone number is 555-0148.

Membership
A household membership costs 75 dollars per year.
Members may bring two adults and all children who live in the same home.
Members do not pay general admission.
The membership desk is just inside the main entrance, next to the blue otter statue.
The statue is a meeting landmark. It is not an exhibit for sale.

Bags and galleries
Large backpacks must be left at the coat desk.
Water bottles with lids are allowed in the galleries.
Food is not allowed in the exhibit halls. Food bought in the cafe must stay in the cafe.
Strollers are allowed in every hall except the Sky Dome during planetarium shows.

Planning facts
Sunday closing time is 5:00 p.m.
Household memberships are sold at the desk beside the blue otter statue.
Visitors call 555-0148 to ask whether a school group still has space.
